From: KOReader <https://github.com/koreader/koreader-base>
Subject: [PATCH] deps: make the WinCrypt/LibreSSL include dance work on Windows

LibreSSL's `ossl_typ.h` undefines the `X509_NAME` & co macros that
`wincrypt.h` defines, but only when `__WINCRYPT_H__` is already defined by
the time it is processed. `openssl/ssl.h` only reaches `winsock2.h` ->
`windows.h` through `dtls1.h`, i.e. too late: the clashing macros are
already in effect while `x509v3.h` is parsed, and the build fails on Windows:

    openssl/x509v3.h:184:17: error: expected specifier-qualifier-list before '(' token
      184 |                 X509_NAME *directoryName;

Include the Win32 headers first on Windows, so LibreSSL can clean up after
them.

--- a/deps/turbo_ffi_wrap.h
+++ b/deps/turbo_ffi_wrap.h
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ limitations under the License. */
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
 #ifndef TURBO_NO_SSL
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#include <winsock2.h>
+#include <windows.h>
+#endif
 #include <openssl/ssl.h>
 #endif
 #include <stdbool.h>
--- a/deps/turbo_ffi_wrap.c
+++ b/deps/turbo_ffi_wrap.c
@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@ SOFTWARE."			*/
 #include "turbo_ffi_wrap.h"
 
 #ifndef TURBO_NO_SSL
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#include <winsock2.h>
+#include <windows.h>
+#endif
 #include <openssl/x509v3.h>
 #include <openssl/ssl.h>
 #endif
